    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (2 tests, the only test class in the project). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` field on the owner API so it returns `SILVER` when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, and `BRONZE` otherwise.\n\nTwo changes, following the project's existing Spring/OpenAPI/MapStruct conventions:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is generated from this spec at build time), documented alongside the existing derived fields like `membershipNumber`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression that derives the tier when mapping `Owner` \u2192 `OwnerDto`, mirroring how `displayName`, `initials`, and `membershipNumber` are already computed:\n   ```java\n   owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0\n       && owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank()\n       ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\"\n   ```\n   The null guards keep it safe for owners created without a namesake count or email (which correctly fall through to `BRONZE`).\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) and the full suite pass with a green build.",
